  "notes": "Issue #605. Follow-up to EXP-516 (ARCHIVE): EXP-516 multiplied balanced_sample_weight by 1.5x for the lowest burden quartile of fold-train regardless of class, which let originally high-burden classes (LUAD -0.064, DLBC -0.050, BLCA -0.050) take the largest collateral damage even though they were never the hypothesis target. This experiment replaces the burden quantile criterion with class membership: only fold-train rows whose train SUBCLASS is one of the 8 pre-declared low-burden/high-misclassification classes (KIRC, KIPAN, GBMLGG, SARC, PRAD, PCPG, THYM, LAML) get an extra 1.2x multiplier on top of the existing balanced_sample_weight. LUAD, BLCA and DLBC are not in this list, so they are not directly targeted, which is expected to structurally block the EXP-516 collateral-damage mechanism. The 8-class list and the 1.2x multiplier were both fixed before this run and are not re-tuned against this run's own OOF result. All EXP-374 features, model hyperparameters, checkpoint policy, folds and seed are unchanged.",
